            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "The intent and overall direction are good \u2014 this is a real footgun and the fix is consistent with the existing per-row root protection already present in editEnable and the table actions column. \nThe biggest concern is the local divergence from the shared selection mixin (even though this file needs to be migrated to use the `useTableSelection` composable instead.)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/UserManagement/UserManagement.vue",
                    "line": 61,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "let the user know why it's disabled.\nAdd a `:title` attribute (or aria-label) when disabled, e.g. $t('pageUserManagement.toast.rootCannotBeSelected') \u2014 \"The root user cannot be included in bulk operations.\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/UserManagement/UserManagement.vue",
                    "line": 61,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Implemented, with a cross-browser follow-up fix.\nAdded disabled-state explanation for root selection and moved tooltip trigger to a non-disabled wrapper so it reliably shows in Edge/Chrome/Firefox (disabled controls do not consistently show native title tooltips).\nAlso added tooltip config and styling to improve readability and avoid clipping."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/UserManagement/UserManagement.vue",
                    "line": 250,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "This is pre-existing, but there are now (with this patch) 5 comparisons to `'root'` on this page (plus 1 in `ModalUser.vue`).  change to an environment variable.  Add a helper to the `userManagment` store `isRootUser(user)`, that returns `'root'` if the env variable does not exist."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/UserManagement/UserManagement.vue",
                    "line": 250,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Implemented. Replaced hardcoded root comparisons with centralized root detection in userManagement store, including env-aware fallback."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/UserManagement/UserManagement.vue",
                    "line": 252,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "I can't follow this.\nreplace with `enabled: !isSelf && !isRoot,`"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/UserManagement/UserManagement.vue",
                    "line": 252,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Implemented. Simplified delete action enable logic to the requested boolean form using local flags."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/UserManagement/UserManagement.vue",
                    "line": 277,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "This function overrides the `BVTableSelectableMixin` but drops `filteredItems` support and post-select reconciliation\n\nin the mixin:\n```\n        const allItems = tableRef.filteredItems || tableRef.items || [];\n        const endIndex = Math.min(startIndex + perPage, allItems.length);\n```\n\n1. Filtering is lost (not a current problem as this page does not use the filter).\n2. Header checkbox state will not be reset because root is intentionally left unselected, the header will stay in indeterminate state after \"select all\" (mixin's `onRowSelected` compares `selectedOnPageCount === pageItemsCount`). That's arguably the correct visual feedback \u2014 but it should be a deliberate design decision, not an emergent one. Add a brief comment explaining \"root is excluded by design, so header may show indeterminate after select-all\" so this is clear.\n3. Pagination removal: The commit message says \"Simplify onChangeHeaderCheckbox by removing unused pagination\". That's true today (no currentPage/perPage props on this <b-table>), but it tightly couples the override to a single page's current state."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/UserManagement/UserManagement.vue",
                    "line": 277,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Implemented. Updated onChangeHeaderCheckbox override to preserve shared mixin behavior:\n\nrestored filteredItems support\nrestored currentPage/perPage windowing\nadded post-select reconciliation via onRowSelected\nadded explicit comment that root is intentionally excluded, so header may remain indeterminate after select-all"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/UserManagement/UserManagement.vue",
                    "line": 280,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "This line is long, is prettier not being run on the commit hook?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/UserManagement/UserManagement.vue",
                    "line": 280,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Implemented. Broke the long conditional line into formatter-friendly multiline style."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/UserManagement/UserManagement.vue",
                    "line": 353,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "This is a little bit unexpected, to clear the selection after deleting a single user.  It seems defensive.  If it can't be addressed here please add a comment here explaining why."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/UserManagement/UserManagement.vue",
                    "line": 353,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Implemented. Removed defensive clearSelectedRows from single-user delete flow so row-action delete does not unexpectedly clear existing bulk selection."
                }
